  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the rhetorical question text",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the bottom textual material which poses the rhetorical question 'donald trumps wall doesn't seem so stupid now does it?'. This projection invites the user to identify with the speaker of the rhetorical question, encouraging them to adopt the meme's perspective that the wall was a necessary or obvious response to the Paris attack. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the rhetorical structure and the framing of the question create an implicit projection of the user as the one being asked to agree or reflect on the implied conclusion.",
